MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C: <EDH>
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_001: Well, hello, Theodora. All alone today? Is something\nthe matter?
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_002: I noticed your absence and came looking for you.\nWhere have you been?
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_003: Here and there, attending to soldiers and refugees.\nThe same work I do with the people of the forest.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_004: They're pressing on with their lives, despite\neverything. Things are fine for now.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_005: You have spent many, many years watching over\nus this way.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_006: Since the founding of Damascar...or perhaps long\nbefore that.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_007: Yes. Ever since the White Egg descended in\nthis land.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_008: I was there for the fall of Damascar, and I was there\nto see Saramis flourish to this very day.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_009: I've seen people born, mature, and depart this life.\nSo trust me when I say you've become a fine queen.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_010: Hm. I suppose.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_011: Er, is something wrong?
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_012: I was considering the wealth of history you must\nhave witnessed.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_013: For you...a single life, even my own, passes in the\nblink of an eye.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_014: And so I wondered if you see me as simply another\nchild of the White Egg you are bound to protect.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_015: Not at all.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_016: There are few I consider myself closer to, in all my\nlong life, than House Savangren.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_017: While I do feel duty bound to the prisoners of\nDagsion for failing to stop Damascar's destruction...
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_018: I've paid special attention to the people of the forest\nover the centuries. Especially Saramis.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_019: I really do feel like an auntie now. This must be what\nit's like for an elder relative.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_020: So wipe away that frown. Alright?
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_021: That's not what I meant though.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_022: I...fear being lost to the flow of time. I want to have\na place in your heart.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_023: Not as a member of House Savangren, but as me.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_024: Oh, Theodora...
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_025: I think of you as a friend. One of the few that I have.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_026: Hehe. You know, we haven't talked as much ever\nsince you took command at Fort Zanbar.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_027: But before that—when you were very young—you\nalways clung to me. It was adorable.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_028: "Clung to you"? Surely you exaggerate.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_029: Hahaha. This is why I could never forget you.\nNot until my end.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_030: Very well. I am relieved to hear it.
MID_SE_Seo_Tro_C_031: I say this not as a queen but as a friend...\nthank you, Troy.